# Tor for net/ (vpn). Installed as /etc/tor/torrc by install.sh net,
# which keeps the User and DataDirectory lines of the torrc that was
# there. The vpn service starts Tor right after OpenVPN, so Tor always
# goes out through the VPN (straight out only in level 0 and the
# sandbox).

# proxychains (proxychains program)
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
# the browser: its own port, so its own circuits and exits, and
# sites can't link it to what proxychains runs
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9150
# the system's DNS: resolv.conf says 127.0.0.1 and the firewall sends
# port 53 here (not 53 itself, so Tor needs no root for it)
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:9053
# vpn level 3 (everything through Tor) and .onion addresses
TransPort 127.0.0.1:9040
# .onion names get a fake address from this range; the firewall sends
# connections to it into Tor, so onion sites work in every program
AutomapHostsOnResolve 1
VirtualAddrNetworkIPv4 10.192.0.0/10

ClientUseIPv6 0
AvoidDiskWrites 1
SafeLogging 1
# warnings only, in /run (gone after a reboot)
Log warn file /run/vpn/tor.log
